<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Margaret, Countess of Comminges</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1363–<a href="/years/1443">1443</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Marguerite of Comminges</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Margaret was countess of Comminges from childhood until her death in 1443, the last of the line of counts. Her three marriages, the third to Mathieu de Foix, led to long disputes over her inheritance, and she spent many years imprisoned by her last husband. After her death the county passed to the French crown, and Charles VII annexed it in 1454.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Charles IV’s alliance with the Habsburgs and with Louis XIII’s rebellious brother Gaston of Orléans, who secretly married the duke’s sister <b>Marguerite</b>, provoked French invasion in 1633; the duchy was occupied for most of the next three decades and ravaged by war, plague and famine.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-lorraine">Duchy of Lorraine · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The comital line ended with Countess <b>Marguerite</b>, whose disputed inheritance was settled in favour of the crown; Charles VII annexed Comminges to the Kingdom of France in 1454.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-comminges">County of Comminges</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=46.58,0.34&amp;year=1415" aria-label="Poitiers on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4558 526 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Margaret, Countess of Comminges"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5008 796h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5008 796h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=46.58,0.34&amp;year=1415">What was here in 1415? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
